id: pm-ado-ns93
title: Reject cross-organization and imprecise Azure DevOps relation targets
description: "mapRelations currently reduces any relation URL to its numeric final segment. A cross-organization link ending in a local work-item ID can be misrepresented as a local PM dependency, and a numeric segment above Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER is rounded into another ID. Validate the canonical same-organization Azure DevOps work-item URL and safe integer identity before mapping; report rejected links as unmapped."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-26T18:03:42.802Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-26T18:08:58.862Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#712c633aeba880b87637647b"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Cross-organization, non-work-item, and unsafe-integer relation targets are refused without silently creating PM links; valid organization URLs retain all existing known relation kinds; package release gate and strict PM health pass."
parent: pm-ado-g4v1
severity: high
repro_steps: "Call mapRelations with a relation URL from another organization ending in /workItems/12, or call relationTargetId with /workItems/9007199254740993."
expected_result: Only same-organization work-item URLs with positive safe integer IDs become PM links; rejected links remain visible in unmapped output.
actual_result: "Any URL with a numeric final segment is mapped, including foreign organization URLs and rounded large IDs."
affected_version: 2026.9.2
component: relations
